---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { catalog, watchlist, path, dateLabel } from '../../lib/catalog';
---

<Base
  title="How the field guide works"
  description="Our approach to San Francisco burrito research: sources, review labels, branch-specific orders, posted hours, uncertainties and updates."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">GOOD BURRITOS. RECEIPTS INCLUDED.</p>
      <h1>
        A guide with
        <br />
        <em>a paper trail.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="dek">
        A starting point for your own opinions, built from critical reviews, restaurant information
        and a little curiosity about the whole city.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="page-body prose reading-width">
      <h2>What makes the cut?</h2>
      <p>
        This is a curated research catalog, not an exhaustive census or a firsthand tasting ranking.
        We look for respectable burritos across San Francisco: Mission standards, fries-inside
        California versions, breakfast, seafood and meat alternatives. The source matters as much as
        the recommendation.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Burrito review:</strong> independent criticism specifically discussing the
          burrito.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Restaurant coverage:</strong> broader coverage of the restaurant or its tacos,
          paired with current menu information. It is not a burrito verdict.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Archive pick:</strong> an older burrito review. A useful lead, with no claim that
          today’s experience is unchanged.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Neighborhood candidate:</strong> menu or local evidence supports inclusion;
          dedicated burrito criticism is still missing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>History stop:</strong> a place in the city’s burrito story, distinguished from a
          current critical recommendation.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>A branch is a branch.</h2>
      <p>
        Orders, reviews and descriptions of the setting apply to the location explicitly identified.
        Extra branches have their own address and hours. A review of the Mission flagship does not
        become a review of every other location.
      </p>
      <p>
        “Source summary” means a description drawn from a cited source. “Format inference” means an
        interpretation of the venue format. Neither claims we visited.
      </p>
      <h2>Hours, honestly.</h2>
      <p>
        Schedules are posted hours in <code>America/Los_Angeles</code>, not real-time availability.
        Restaurant hours, kitchen hours, online ordering and truck schedules are labeled separately.
        Unknown days stay unknown, conflicts stay visible, and overnight windows say “next day.”
        Check the operator before a special trip.
      </p>
      <p>
        “Listed” means a source lists that location. “Published” means the source supplies a
        complete weekly schedule. Neither label establishes that the doors are open right now.
      </p>
      <h2>When was this checked?</h2>
      <p>
        The catalog snapshot is <strong>{dateLabel(catalog.updated_on)}</strong>. Each source
        records a research date and, when known, a publication date. A recent research date does not
        turn an old review into a new tasting. This is a maintained repository, not a live
        restaurant feed.
      </p>
      <h2>About the map.</h2>
      <p>
        73 of the 80 listed location records have an exact address match from the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography/technical-documentation/complete-technical-documentation/census-geocoder.html">
          U.S. Census Bureau Geocoder
        </a>
        . Those points are interpolated along address ranges, so they are approximate positions, not
        verified entrances or proof of a business’s presence. Seven unmatched or truck locations
        remain accessible in the list. Background maps are from{' '}
        <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>.
      </p>
      <h2 id="watchlist">On the watchlist.</h2>
      <p>
        These leads have no confirmed opening or reopening. They are excluded from the 56 catalog
        and history stops and from the active map.
      </p>
      <ul>
        {watchlist.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={path(`places/${p.id}/`)}>{p.name}</a> — {p.summary}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <h2>Help keep it useful.</h2>
      <p>
        Found a changed menu, a closure, or a missing contender?{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/mldangelo/burrito/issues/new">Open a GitHub issue</a> with a
        source and the exact branch. The{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/mldangelo/burrito">public repository</a> contains the complete
        JSON catalog, schemas, research notes and build code.{' '}
        <a href={path('data/')}>Browse the data exports.</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
